    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0571" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11478.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-12T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At about 10.15 yesterday morning while on duty ashore at the post office building
                    here a mail orderly from the <hi rendition="#italic">Minnesota</hi> in full
                    uniform with the official mail bag across his shoulder was arrested by a
                    policeman at the orders of Mexican soldier and taken to the jail. After being
                    questioned the jefe político released the orderly and locked up the soldier. I
                    shall investigate the matter and report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
